, "Article 22A UK GDPR", "Awaab's Law", "social housing repairs AI", "ICO agentic AI", "AI triage housing association", "meaningful human involvement", "durable workflows Dapr", "fractional CTO United Kingdom", "AI agents public services"], "faq": [["What changed in UK law on automated decisions?", "The Data (Use and Access) Act 2025 replaced Article 22 of the UK GDPR with new Articles 22A to 22D, in force from 5 February 2026. Solely automated significant decisions are generally permitted with safeguards, such as information about the decision, a way to contest it and human intervention, with tighter limits where special category data is involved."], ["What is Awaab's Law?", "A legal requirement for social landlords in England to investigate and fix damp, mould and other serious hazards within set timescales. Its first phase, covering damp and mould and emergency hazards, came into force in October 2025."], ["Should AI agents decide repair priorities on their own?", "In this design, rules set statutory priorities, the agent classifies and drafts, and people make decisions that significantly affect tenants. That keeps the system fast and within the safeguards the law expects."]], "related": ["/fractional-cto-united-kingdom/", "/ai-architect/", "/fractional-cto/"], "citations": [{"title": "One year on: marking the 12-month commencement of the Data (Use and Access) Act", "url": "https://ico.org.uk/about-the-ico/media-centre/news-and-blogs/2026/06/one-year-on-marking-the-12-month-commencement-of-the-data-use-and-access-act/", "publisher": "ICO", "date": "Jun 2026"}, {"title": "UK: Commencement of the data protection provisions in the Data (Use and Access) Act", "url": "https://privacymatters.dlapiper.com/2026/02/uk-commencement-of-the-data-protection-provisions-in-the-data-use-and-access-act/", "publisher": "DLA Piper", "date": "Feb 2026"}, {"title": "AI and Automated Decision-Making in the UK (Part I): The new rules and regulatory guidance", "url": "https://www.hlc.co